        name = "Tabard of the Earthen Ring",
        stepCount = 5,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Needs initial reputation and underwater travel; the vendor is inside a cave above the seabed.\n\n1. Check The Earthen Ring in your reputation panel. If you are already Friendly from Deepholm, Vashj'ir or other Earthen Ring quests, you can go directly to the vendor once you can travel underwater safely. You do not have to finish Vashj'ir's entire campaign.\n\n2. For a fresh route, start Vashj'ir from your capital's Cataclysm introduction: Naraat the Earthspeaker at 74.6,19.6 in Stormwind or Farseer Krogar at 50.6,38.6 in Orgrimmar. Follow the Vashj'ir/Call of Duty chain, board its ship and allow the shipwreck sequence to finish. An already unlocked Vashj'ir portal can be used instead.\n\n3. In Kelp'thar Forest, complete Sea Legs with Erunak Stonespeaker around 45.1,23.5 for underwater breathing and movement. Follow the survivors' opening quests. Complete Moanah Stormhoof's The Abyssal Ride around 46.0,46.8 if you want the fast zone seahorse, then continue Earthen Ring quest rewards until Friendly. Reputation previously earned in Deepholm also counts.\n\n4. Travel into the Shimmering Expanse and approach Silver Tide Hollow near 50.5,38.0. Face south toward the reef column and look for the cave mouth partway above the seabed, among the conspicuous yellow/purple coral fronds. Swim into the side of the reef; swimming along the surface or standing on top of the vendor's map dot will not enter the refuge.\n\n5. Inside the air-filled cave, find Provisioner Arok near 49.0,42.0 on the Shimmering Expanse map, beside the other camp vendors. This refuge does not require completing every quest leading to it. Buy Tabard of the Earthen Ring (65905) for up to 1 gold once Friendly, then equip it.",
