        stepCount = 8,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - A fresh character must advance a long campaign through several quest chains before the initially hostile faction will sell anything.\n\n1. If D'lom is already friendly and your Therazane reputation is Friendly or higher, skip to step 8. Otherwise start The Maelstrom with Naraat the Earthspeaker at 74.6,19.6 in Stormwind or Farseer Krogar at 50.6,38.6 in Orgrimmar. Follow the portal/flight introduction into Deepholm; an already unlocked Deepholm portal also works.\n\n2. At the Temple of Earth around 49.5,53.3 in Deepholm, follow the World Pillar recovery story. Complete the Stormcaller Mylra/airship chain and the Stonehearth/Earthen chain that restore the first two required fragments. Return the fragments and turn in their Temple follow-ups. Flying straight to Therazane's Throne on a fresh character does not bypass this progression.\n\n3. Take The Very Earth Beneath Our Feet (26326) when the Temple story offers it. Meet Earthcaller Torunscar and Earthmender Norsala northwest of the Temple near 46.0,45.6. Complete Crumbling Defenses, Core of Our Troubles and On Even Ground, then Imposing Confrontation. Read the proclamation to Boden and stay in front of him until his speech and knockback finish; leaving early can prevent quest credit.\n\n4. Take Rocky Relations to Diamant the Patient at 56.4,42.6. Complete Hatred Runs Deep, Unsolid Ground and Loose Stones, then the follow-ups through Violent Gale, Depth of the Depths and A Rock Amongst Many. Take Entrenched when offered; it sends you to Kor the Immovable at 34.4,34.4. The Stonecore dungeon detour is not needed just for this tabard.\n\n5. At Kor, complete the offered aid quests and follow-ups through Clingy, So Big, So Round... and Rock Bottom. When Pebble offers Petrified Delicacies, gather 12 Petrified Stone Bats; ground pickups around 42.8,29.4 can supply them without repeatedly killing basilisks. Turn the bats in to Pebble, then check Kor again for the next handoffs. Keep both the main story and Pebble's follow-up moving if one seems to stop.\n\n6. Follow Steady Hand to Terrath at 39.8,19.5 in the Pale Roost and complete his branch through Resonating Blow. Follow Rocky Upheaval to Gorsik at 72.2,53.8 in the Crimson Expanse and complete his offered fungal/corruption branch, including its follow-ups to Shaken and Stirred and Corruption Destruction. Finish the outstanding handoffs on both sides until At the Stonemother's Call (26750) becomes available.\n\n7. Speak to Therazane at her northern throne around 56.3,12.2 and finish the offered story handoffs until the reputation panel shows at least Friendly and D'lom is a friendly vendor. Check him at this point. Unlocking all daily quests, finishing The Binding or completing the Deepholm quest-count achievement is not required just to buy the tabard.\n\n8. At Therazane's Throne, find D'lom the Collector at 56.8,13.2. Buy Tabard of Therazane (65907) for up to 1 gold and equip it. If D'lom remains hostile, resume the outstanding stone-lord story handoff instead of trying to farm dungeon reputation before owning the tabard.",
