        stepCount = 5,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - A guaranteed low-cost purchase after the zone introduction and several Wildhammer quest hubs.\n\n1. Use an Alliance character and check Wildhammer Clan reputation. If already Friendly and Thundermar's quartermaster is accessible, skip to step 5. Hinterlands Wildhammer lore and the Horde's Dragonmaw standing do not replace this Cataclysm reputation.\n\n2. Start the current Twilight Shores introduction with Grand Admiral Jes-Tereth in Stormwind Keep at 85.8,32.4, then meet Fargo Flintlocke at the harbor around 26.1,47.2 and take his seaplane. The old detective quests with young Anduin and King Varian are no longer the Retail entry route. If Fargo is missing, resolve a conflicting Call of Duty harbor phase before returning.\n\n3. At Highbank in Twilight Highlands, around 81.0,79.4, follow Welcome to Highbank!, Burnin' at Both Ends and Aiming High. Continue Kurdran's and Lieutenant Emry's beach quests through Wings Over Highbank, Any Portal in a Storm and The Way is Open. This establishes the Alliance base and its return portal; simply flying to an unopened Highbank can leave the necessary NPCs phased out.\n\n4. Follow the Firebeard's Patrol handoff northwest from Highbank, around 60.2,57.8, and help the Wildhammer families. Complete the offered clan-aid quests, checking Wildhammer Clan reputation in the rewards, and follow the story toward Thundermar. Continue until at least Friendly; you do not need Exalted, the entire zone achievement or the full wedding/daily-quest unlock just to own the tabard.\n\n5. Find Craw McGraw in Thundermar at 48.6,30.6 on the Twilight Highlands map. Buy Tabard of the Wildhammer Clan (65908) for up to 1 gold, then equip it. If it is red, check your actual Wildhammer standing; if the town is still in a story phase, finish its outstanding main handoff and return.",
