        name = "Tabard of the Dragonmaw Clan",
        stepCount = 5,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Requires the Horde zone introduction, a faction uprising and Friendly reputation; capital-city phasing can add a prerequisite.\n\n1. Use a Horde character and check Dragonmaw Clan reputation. If already Friendly and the Bloodgulch vendor is accessible, skip to step 5. This is the Twilight Highlands faction, not Netherwing in Outland, and the tabard does not unlock Netherwing drakes.\n\n2. In Orgrimmar, speak to Eitrigg inside Grommash Hold around 49.0,72.8 and begin Machines of War. Follow the preparation quests, including the Azshara fleet/air-force errands, until the chain sends you to Twilight Highlands. Do not wait for the removed original Garrosh version or assume the notice board must display the breadcrumb.\n\n3. At Dragonmaw Port on the eastern coast, around 75.2,54.8, complete the arrival and uprising story with Zaela, including You Say You Want a Revolution and its follow-ups through Return to the Highlands. The chain establishes friendly Dragonmaw control and the capital portal. Flying straight into the hostile initial port does not complete this unlock.\n\n4. Follow Zaela's Northern/Southern Flank quests and the subsequent Dragonmaw work toward Bloodgulch, around 54.8,44.0. Continue reputation-awarding Dragonmaw quests until Friendly. You do not need the Crucible of Carnage arena chain to unlock Grot Deathblow; the faction-page replies explicitly correct that older detour.\n\n5. Find Grot Deathblow at 53.8,42.0 in Bloodgulch, near its flight master. He is inland, not the vendor at Dragonmaw Port. Buy Tabard of the Dragonmaw Clan (65909) for up to 1 gold and equip it. The often-quoted 95-silver price is the Friendly reputation discount on its 1-gold base price.",
